    "name": "Zenith System 3 (19-inch, 1980)",
    "description": "A 19-inch Zenith System 3 table set of the 1980 line (L1960P9, Sams 1891-2) fed by the NES RF modulator on channel 3 through a short cable and an RF switch. Tri-focus in-line gun 100-degree tube with phosphor stripes (reported), no comb filter (Zenith's glass-delay-line comb arrived with the 1981 line), the sharpness control at its detent, Color Sentry holding tint and contrast, white set cool as the factory did. Sound: one PM speaker on a 2 W module, no tone controls; the set's intercarrier detector passes the picture as buzz at an assumed 42 dB AM rejection. Stripe pitch, bandwidths, spot and speaker are class estimates.",
